    "created_at": "2016-05-08T07:41:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-08T07:41:38Z",
    "body": "> the solution is also the same; use `<![CDATA[` ... `]]>`\n\nSure, but the question is whether we are doing the best thing for author-developers by requiring them to do that, or whether at this point we would be helping them more by not requiring it.\n\n> Maybe you can special-case the message in v.nu for SVG script/style?\n\nThat would take a lot of ugly hackery, since the message is emitted by the HTML parser. I would need to make the validator code do a string-match for all the error messages emitted by the HTML parser, to try to catch that one message and special-case it just when there’s an open SVG `script` element.\n\nBut anyway, although the v.nu issue is what led me to propose this parsing change, I would be fine if the resolution is that we don’t want to change it. I didn’t propose it specifically because I don’t want to have to deal with it in v.nu , but instead because I am wondering if the current parsing behavior per spec here is actually the best thing for users or not.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
